      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], here\u0027s how the Hub protects the Anthropic API key:\n\n**The Hub never holds the key in its own process environment at all.** Instead, a local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\nThis design means a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API. The Query agent uses the same scoping model: it receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from or stored in the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
      "input_tokens": 5372,
      "output_tokens": 185
    }
